---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { u } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="GDPR & data processing — Airmino"
  description="How Airmino handles personal data: minimization, VPC/self-hosted deployment, retention, subprocessors, and your rights under the GDPR."
  canonicalPath="/gdpr/"
>
  <div class="gdpr-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="crumb">
        <a href={u('/')}>Home</a>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <span>GDPR &amp; data processing</span>
      </div>
      <div class="kicker">Compliance</div>
      <h1>Your data stays yours.</h1>
      <p>
        Airmino is decision infrastructure, not a data business. We process the minimum personal data
        needed to return a decision, we never train models on your data, and you can keep everything
        inside your own network. Last updated: October 2026.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap gdpr-grid">
      <div class="gdpr-block">
        <h2>What we process</h2>
        <p>
          To return a decision we process the fields you send in <code>POST /v1/decide</code> —
          typically a decision name, the options you define, and context fields (e.g. amounts,
          priorities, segments). What you put in the payload is what gets processed; nothing more
          is collected. Send reference IDs instead of raw personal data wherever your workflow allows it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="gdpr-block">
        <h2>Where it runs</h2>
        <p>
          Airmino deploys inside your VPC or fully self-hosted as a single container with no external
          calls — decision payloads never leave your network and there is no cross-border transfer to
          manage. On the managed cloud option, processing stays in the region you select and logs are
          retained for 30 days, then deleted.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="gdpr-block">
        <h2>No training on your data</h2>
        <p>
          Customer payloads and decisions are never used to train, fine-tune, or evaluate models.
          Product telemetry (request counts, latency distributions, error rates) contains no payload
          content and is aggregated before storage.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="gdpr-block">
        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under the GDPR you can request access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability, and objection for personal data we process as a processor. Because most deployments keep data inside your own infrastructure, many requests are fastest answered by your own team — we support you with deletion tooling and a data processing agreement on request.</p>
        <p>To exercise your rights, contact <a href="mailto:privacy@airmino.com">privacy@airmino.com</a>. We respond within 30 days.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gdpr-block">
        <h2>Subprocessors &amp; DPA</h2>
        <p>
          Self-hosted and VPC deployments have no subprocessors — there is nobody downstream to list.
          The managed cloud option uses only infrastructure hosting in your selected region.
          The trial signup form is processed by FormSubmit (form-to-email delivery) — the only
          website subprocessor. A data processing agreement (DPA) incorporating the EU Standard
          Contractual Clauses where relevant is available on request before any pilot.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="gdpr-block">
        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          Encryption in transit (TLS 1.2+) and at rest, mTLS service identity between components,
          and append-only audit logs for decision traces. Full control mappings are provided under NDA
          during enterprise evaluation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href={u('/usage/')} data-event="gdpr-see-usage">See what it decides →</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={u('/#pricing')} data-event="cta-pricing">See platform pricing</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .gdpr-hero {
    padding: 64px 0 44px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--paper-2);
  }
  .gdpr-hero .crumb a {
    color: var(--muted-2);
  }
  .gdpr-hero .crumb a:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .gdpr-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.6vw, 42px);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    line-height: 1.15;
    font-weight: 680;
  }
  .gdpr-hero p {
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 680px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .gdpr-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 18px;
  }
  .gdpr-block {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 26px;
  }
  .gdpr-block:first-child {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }
  .gdpr-block h2 {
    font-size: 17px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    font-weight: 680;
  }
  .gdpr-block p {
    font-size: 14.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .gdpr-block p + p {
    margin-top: 10px;
  }
  .gdpr-block code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    background: var(--paper-2);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .gdpr-block a {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .gdpr-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
